            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Jillian"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great dressing - definitely clean and simple. It's perfect over mixed greens. I did add a bit of minced garlic as I just love the stuff and a pinch or two of sugar but other that this a very good salad dressing to highlight a good quality balsamic."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "ClassyIce7847"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great but be careful to use a very good aged quality balsamic vinegar. Many cheaper brands are too pungent. If that’s all you can get, add a bit of brown sugar to the vinegar to lower the raw vinegar taste. Aged Balsamic is actually slightly sweet and very thick and a little bit goes a long way.",
            "datePublished": "2022-10-20T23:34:47.032Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Nicole Vorpagel"
            },
            "reviewBody": "great basic dressing you can do a lot with. I gave it 4 instead of 5 because I made a few changes that gave it a little more pazzaz but it's all about personal taste. If you are interested here is what I changed. Equal parts EVOO and vinegar because I felt it was a little too oily in the original, whole garlic clove fresh oregano and I put it in a magic bullet type blender type blender. I think next time I will add fresh basil in too. All in all small changes to a great dressing!",
            "datePublished": "2012-08-21T13:38:56.950Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "bignosekate"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Love this salad dressing. It has the perfect ratio. I use a full tsp GREEK (the best) oregano (check your local Greek specialty food shop for freshly dried oregano). I also add a pinch of sugar whenever I'm making caprese salad for a sweeter dressing. Yum!",
            "datePublished": "2010-04-24T22:57:51.283Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Chels"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really good! I took some other reviewer's suggestions and did 3 T olive oil, 2 T balsamic, 1 T water, 1/2 teaspoon dried oregano, 1/4 teaspoon garlic salt, and a dash of salt and dash of pepper. Lovely! Thank you for this quick salad dressing!!",
            "datePublished": "2014-04-01T06:54:20.807Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gemini1412"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a great base to build on. I doubled it, added basil, sugar and food processed some roasted garlic, roasted red bell pepper and feta and blended till smooth. OUTSTANDING.",
            "datePublished": "2009-07-13T12:30:59.243Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Susan Emma"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fabulous! I scaled up to 9 servings. Put everything in a jar, adding a couple drops of stevia and a mere tad of garlic powder, then shook the jar vigorously. It tastes better as it sits at room temp for even a day or two. No need to refrigerate, since there are no raw ingredients in it. Best dressing I've made in a while.",
            "datePublished": "2016-04-12T16:45:04.593Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "tInA*671*"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great starter recipe! I used some red wine vinegar along with the balsamic and it gave just enough bite.",
            "datePublished": "2010-02-15T15:06:21.587Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MEDFORD63"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I actually use this recipe as a base. I usually don't measure the amount of vinegar and oil I use, I just eyeball it. I also like to add salt and pepper, some dijon mustard and sugar. I love the addition of oregano in this recipe. I usually make this in a jar or other sealed container and then just shake it really hard until it blends together. It's easier than trying to whisk it hard enough to make it emulsify.",
            "datePublished": "2007-04-01T14:54:44.460Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shauna Leigh"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I first made this, as written, because I was short on ingredients and time. I was surprised at how much I liked it, but I'm a big fan of balsamic vinegar. It's a perfect dressing for a weekday, on-the-go salad just for me. I have taken to adding garlic powder and crushed red pepper to it, just to personalize it. Toss it with some greens and feta cheese and I'm a happy little camper.",
            "datePublished": "2015-05-19T01:58:47.927Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
